            "review_title": "Review at Yen Sao Khanh Hoa",
            "review_text": "Picky-trave\nAllentown6 contributions\n0\nPickytrave\nJan 2016 • Family\nOur resort driver recommended this place as good place to dine for seafood and also a nice place on the beach. We went there and was disappointed. The restaurant was an outdoor restaurant but it was dirty. The menu looked nice with color pictures of the dishes, however, when we ordered, we were told they didn't have the dishes or the food was not in season. We saw a grilled lobster dish that looked good but price was not quoted. We asked and we were told the lobsters were sold by weight and would cost $148 US dollars per pound!!!! We were like, Really? In US, lobsters cost from $6 (in season) to $12 (out of season) per lb. I don't think lobsters cost that much in VN, but not sure how they came up with that price! \n\nWe ended up ordering a few dishes to eat, but I had to make sure I asked for the cost of each dish before I ordered (even for those dishes already had the prices listed). I also kept a mental note of the dish prices and checked the bill at the end for accuracy. I wouldn't come back to this restaurant, as I don't think they were honest with their food prices. If you decide to check it out for yourself, make sure you don't get charged an arm and a leg before you order, make a mental note of the food prices, and check your bill to ensure you're not overcharged!\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 24, 2016",
